  "says": "The radial wheel (Ordaen/wheel.luna): each slice of a ring of n in the bank stone (radial-wedge-n), the slice aimed at lit over it (radial-lit-n), the inner edge of a slice's band (radial-arc-n), a band's segment 1/m of a turn wide (radial-band-m, white, tinted), the round middle (radial-middle), and an icon's hollow carved into the stone (radial-carve, radial-carve-lit aimed at). Each is the shape straight up from the wheel's middle, cut to its box and stretched to a power of two; the wheel turns the box about its middle to stand it at its item.",
